    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipesummary|category=Side dish recipes\n| Yield = 2 quarts (liters)|servings=8|time=30 minutes|difficulty=2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Breakfast|Breakfast]] | [[Cookbook:Side dishes|Side dishes]] | [[Cookbook:Native American cuisine|Native American cuisine]]\n\nRecipe from Effigy Mounds National Monument.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*5 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Hominy|hominy]] [[Cookbook:Grits|grits]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]], [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]], or [[Cookbook:Maple Syrup|maple syrup]] (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n#Bring water to a rapid [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]].\n#Gradually stir in the hominy grits.\n#Reduce heat to low.\n#Stir in the butter.\n#Cook for 20 minutes, or until the water is absorbed.\n#If desired, sweeten with honey, brown sugar, maple syrup, or jelly. \n#Serve while hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Grits can also be flavored with [[Cookbook:Cheese|cheese]], sunny-side up egg, or small bits of [[Cookbook:Ham|ham]] or [[Cookbook:Sausage|sausage]].\n\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn]]\n[[Category:Native American recipes]]\n[[Category:North American recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hominy]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]",
